<title>USA: Replacement workers &quot;down the road issue&quot; -- UPS.</title>
<headline>Replacement workers &quot;down the road issue&quot; -- UPS.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The possibility of hiring replacements for striking Teamsters workers was something that United Parcel Service was hoping to avoid but would consider if necessary in the future, a UPS spokeswoman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Our hope is that our people come back to work. The last thing that we want to do is hire replacement workers,&quot; UPS Vice President for Human Resources Lea Soupata said. &quot;The striker replacement issue is a down the road issue,&quot; she added.</p>
<p>((Washington newsroom, 202 898-8300))</p>
